# Closed references by name are no error (the author 2026-11-11; plan M11 5a): A holds the atom B, B holds the atom A,
# and a path through them goes round -- A\B is B, A\B\A is A, A\B\A\B is B; nothing is expanded, so nothing loops and
# the dump prints both blocks as written.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and reads
# the Structures by paths through main\data. main has no code, so there is no call: its part code is the empty `()`.
sub: main () (
    A:
        int: v 1
        B
    B:
        int: v 2
        A
) ()
int: seen main\data\A\B\A\B\v
